# Line-ending normalisation. Added 2026-09-17 on Al's instruction.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Before this file, core.autocrlf was false with no
# normalisation, on a Windows working copy inside OneDrive. Any tool that
# rewrote a file with different line endings produced a whole-file diff, so
# `git status --porcelain` reported nine modified files when the real change
# count was zero. SYNC.md names that command as the one cheap check against
# clone drift, so the only safeguard in this repo was returning false
# positives every time and no true ones. A check that always fires is not a
# check.
#
# Text is stored LF in the repo and checked out per platform.

* text=auto

# Binaries. Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is text and should diff as text.
*.svg text

# Scripts, pinned. Batch files are run on Windows and keep CRLF; shell
# scripts keep LF or they fail on the runner.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
